# Olmedo et al., TOPLAS 2018, Example 4.9 (p. 4:20): a fair coin chooses between diverging and
# tossing two fair coins (0 is heads) observed to show at least one head.  The probability that
# the last toss is heads is 2/7 under cwp, 6/7 under cwlp and 2/3 under r2.
# Expected: not valid (cwlp is 6/7 > 0.85).  The reduction asks the lower bound
# wp_(1-q)(S, 1 - [y = 0]) >= 1 - q for q = 0.85, and 0.14375 < 0.15.
nat x;
nat y;
{
	while (true) {
		skip;
	}
}[1/2]{
	{
		x := 0;
	}[1/2]{
		x := 1;
	}
	{
		y := 0;
	}[1/2]{
		y := 1;
	}
	observe(x = 0 || y = 0);
}
?Ex [[y = 0]] <= 0.85 cwlp
